{"items":[{"path":"tools.openchamber","description":"OpenChamber projects, sessions and worktrees. One action per call; projectId or directory scope it, default this session's directory. A session you create, send to or fork belongs to the user, who follows and talks to it. Dispatch one when the user asks, even for work related to yours, with any agent, optionally in a new worktree. A session you start to get work done and collect its answer takes ownWork, also when the user told you to delegate; smaller pieces go to the subagent tool. A dispatch returns at once; returnResult brings its final answer back here as a message. session.send always starts a new prompt. session.moveToWorktree moves this session into a new worktree on a new branch from the default branch, taking the changed files you name in carry. It can help when the checkout looks busy: someone's pull request branch, uncommitted changes, another session here, a branch changed between your messages. Whether that fits depends on how the user works: ask, unless the request already calls for separate work, such as a pull request of its own. Unlike git worktree add, the session moves along and the branch starts from the default branch. This tool cannot delete sessions or worktrees.","signature":"tools.openchamber({
  /**
   * OpenChamber action to perform (projects.list: Projects and Chats; use an id as projectId for session.create. No parameters; models.list: Default, favorite and recent models; no parameters; models.search: The model catalog, favorites and recent models first; optional query, provider, all, limit, offset; session.list: Newest top-level sessions here; each has inWork (in the sidebar's In work) and doneSuggested (its last turn looks finished). Filters inWork, busy (running now), mine (sessions you created with ownWork, with their status), query (title words); inWork, busy and mine span every project unless scoped and return all matches. Optional limit, all, children, withStatus (status as in session.status); session.archive: Archive sessionId, a session you created with ownWork, once you used its result. Restoring one is the user's; session.markDone: Take sessionId (default: this session) out of In work, as the Done button does. Only on the user's word; a later message puts it back; session.track: Put sessionId back in In work, as the Track button does, such as to undo a markDone; session.create: In this directory by default; projectId from projects.list selects a project or openchamber:chats for a new Chat. Use the returned directory for later session actions. Prompt optional; session.send: New prompt to sessionId; session.fork: Fork sessionId at messageId; prompt optional; session.status: Status of sessionId: busy, idle, or waiting when it cannot go on until the user answers it. An unknown id is an error; session.messages: Text messages and sessionStatus of sessionId; session.moveToWorktree: Move sessionId (default: this session) and its carry files into a new worktree, made the way the New worktree dialog makes one; requires worktree. Nothing moves when carry cannot be applied; directory is ignored; session.link: Add link to sessionId (default: this session); the same link again updates its title; session.unlink: Remove a link from sessionId (default: this session), named by the url or identifier it was linked with; wait.list: This session's waits, and the sources to wait on (the built-in timer, pull requests, and what extensions offer), with the args each takes; wait.start: Requires source and args: "timer" with { "minutes": N } (1 to 1440); "pr" with { "url": "<GitHub pull request or GitLab merge request address>" }, which wakes the session when a check fails or every check passes, someone comments or reviews, the branch conflicts or falls behind, or it is merged or closed; or a source from wait.list with args as its params say. Each pull request is its own wait, so a session can wait on several. One wake ends the wait, so start it again to keep waiting. End your turn while you wait. Never wait with a sleep loop; wait.stop: Stop waitId (a pull request wait's waitId is its address), or every wait of this session without it; work.name: Name the worktree's or isolated space's task for sessionId (default: this session), never a session; a lead's name is its session title, so for a lead it renames the session. In title: at most 4 words in the user's latest language; rename only for a different task. A user-given name stays. Main checkout and plain folders need no naming. A worktree on an OpenChamber-generated placeholder branch also requires branch, the English branch name after the task, and renames it; any other branch stays; lead.brief: Only in a lead session. Without brief or edits it returns the brief; edits changes parts of it, brief replaces it whole; lead.digest: Only in a lead session. Replaces the digest the user reads above the chat with needsYou, now, news and suggestions; file.open: Put path in front of the user's file panel, for a result worth seeing: a screenshot, report, CSV, recording, generated page)
   */
  action: "projects.list" | "models.list" | "models.search" | "session.list" | "session.archive" | "session.markDone" | "session.track" | "session.create" | "session.send" | "session.fork" | "session.status" | "session.messages" | "session.moveToWorktree" | "session.link" | "session.unlink" | "wait.list" | "wait.start" | "wait.stop" | "work.name" | "lead.brief" | "lead.digest" | "file.open",
  /** Inputs for the action; use an empty object when none are needed */
  parameters?: {
    /** Not with directory */
    projectId?: string,
    /** Absolute path; default: this session's directory */
    directory?: string,
    sessionId?: string,
    /** Fork boundary */
    messageId?: string,
    link?: {
      url: string,
      title: string,
      /** change: pull, merge or change request. issue: task or ticket */
      kind: "change" | "issue",
      /** Short label such as !42 or OPS-7 */
      identifier?: string,
    },
    title?: string,
    prompt?: string,
    /**
     * provider/model. session.create with an agent and no model runs that agent's bound model; with neither, it picks from models.list favorites or recents, or omits it; send and fork omit it to keep the session's model
     */
    model?: string,
    /** Only when the user asks. Default: build for a new session, unchanged for an existing one */
    agent?: string,
    /** Only when the user asks */
    variant?: string,
    /**
     * Folder name of a new worktree, named after the task (fix-login-timeout). Required for session.moveToWorktree; on session.create only when the user asks, and uncommitted changes stay behind
     */
    worktree?: string,
    /** session.create: default the worktree name. work.name: the new name of a placeholder branch */
    branch?: string,
    /** Ref the new branch starts from; default: the repository's default branch */
    startRef?: string,
    /** Files you changed whose uncommitted changes move along; nothing else moves */
    carry?: Array<string>,
    /**
     * Check out this existing local or remote branch (origin/feature) instead of a new one; not with branch or startRef
     */
    existingBranch?: string,
    /** Track the upstream branch */
    setUpstream?: boolean,
    /**
     * session.create only, when the user asks to work on that pull or merge request: the session starts in a new worktree on its branch. worktree and branch then only rename the folder and local branch
     * @integer @minimum 1
     */
    pullRequest?: number,
    /** Goal Mode; only when the user asks */
    goal?: boolean,
    /** Requires goal. @integer @minimum 1000 @maximum 100000000 */
    goalTokenBudget?: number,
    /**
     * create, send or fork with a prompt: the final answer arrives here as a message when the session finishes. Only when the user wants the outcome or your next step needs it
     */
    returnResult?: boolean,
    /**
     * session.create: the session is part of your own task, not one the user asked for. It nests under this session in the sidebar, the user does not talk to it, it cannot ask questions with tools, and with a prompt every answer it ends a turn with comes back here, whatever started that turn (your prompt, its own subagents finishing, a wait firing), until it is archived, unless returnResult is false. Leave it out when the user wants the session for themselves, to follow and talk to
     */
    ownWork?: boolean,
    /** Only the last assistant message */
    lastAssistant?: boolean,
    /** Default 10. @integer @minimum 1 */
    limit?: number,
    /** Include archived sessions, all messages, or older model versions */
    all?: boolean,
    /** Words to match: model names and ids for models.search, session titles for session.list */
    query?: string,
    /** session.list: only sessions in In work */
    inWork?: boolean,
    /** session.list: only sessions running now */
    busy?: boolean,
    /** session.list: include subagent sessions and sessions created with ownWork */
    children?: boolean,
    /** Provider id or name */
    provider?: string,
    /** Results to skip, for the next page. @integer @minimum 0 */
    offset?: number,
    /** Only the last matching message */
    last?: boolean,
    withStatus?: boolean,
    role?: "all" | "user" | "assistant",
    /** Absolute, or relative to the session directory */
    path?: string,
    /** session.unlink: the address of the link to remove */
    url?: string,
    /** session.unlink: the identifier of the link to remove, when no url */
    identifier?: string,
    /** wait.start: "timer", "pr", or <extension>/<wait> as wait.list names it */
    source?: string,
    /**
     * wait.start: the arguments the source's params list, such as { "minutes": 10 } or { "url": "https://github.com/o/r/pull/1" }
     */
    args?: {},
    /** wait.stop: the wait to stop; without it every wait of this session */
    waitId?: string,
    /**
     * lead.brief: the whole brief as markdown, at most 12000 characters: the user's goal and agreed outcomes in their words, rules, and each strand of work with its expected result
     */
    brief?: string,
    /**
     * lead.brief: changes applied in order, each replacing the exact text find, which must appear once, with replace; nothing is saved when one fails
     */
    edits?: Array<{
        find: string,
        replace: string,
      }>,
    /**
     * lead.digest: at most 3 questions to the user, each with up to 4 short options and the recommended one, word for word
     */
    needsYou?: Array<{
        question: string,
        options?: Array<string>,
        recommended?: string,
      }>,
    /** lead.digest: one line per strand of work, where it stands */
    now?: Array<string>,
    /** lead.digest: at most 5 lines, only what changed the picture since the user last wrote */
    news?: Array<string>,
    /** lead.digest: at most 3 lines, work worth doing outside what the user gave you, with why */
    suggestions?: Array<string>,
    /** session.list: only the sessions you created with ownWork, each with its status */
    mine?: boolean,
  },
}): Promise<string | null>"}],"remaining":0,"next":null}

